TEXT 176 -176 Left 3 ;#199 Coil tester on a parallel tuned circuit
TEXT 176 -112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ff5xOENID7w
TEXT 176 -64 Left 2 ;With S1 open the built-in 150 pF is out of circuit and the oscillator runs at the resonance
TEXT 176 -32 Left 2 ;of whatever tuned circuit is connected, which is how an IF transformer gets identified.
TEXT 176 656 Left 2 ;Circuit from "The Coil Tester" by Michael A. Covington, N4TMI,
TEXT 176 688 Left 2 ;73 Magazine, September 1990, page 48. J1 is a source follower and
TEXT 176 720 Left 2 ;J2 a common-gate stage. They share R2, and C2 feeds J2's drain back
TEXT 176 752 Left 2 ;to J1's gate, so the loop only has enough gain to oscillate at resonance.
TEXT 176 800 Left 2 ;Lif and Cif are not parts of the tester. They are the tuned winding and
TEXT 176 832 Left 2 ;the internal capacitor of the transformer under test, 680 uH and 180 pF
TEXT 176 864 Left 2 ;for a 455 kHz can. Lif carries Rser=24, which LTspice does not draw:
TEXT 176 896 Left 2 ;a loaded Q near 80. Rmon stands for the counter across the output jack.
TEXT 1200 -176 Left 2 !.tran 0 2m 0 20n
TEXT 1200 -136 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\Unverified\2N5245_standard_jft.lib
TEXT 1200 -96 Left 2 !.meas tran t1 WHEN V(tank)=0 TD=1.5m RISE=1
TEXT 1200 -56 Left 2 !.meas tran t2 WHEN V(tank)=0 TD=1.5m RISE=11
TEXT 1200 -16 Left 2 !.meas tran fosc PARAM 10/(t2-t1)
TEXT 1200 24 Left 2 !.meas tran vtank_pp PP V(tank) FROM 1.5m TO 2m
TEXT 1200 64 Left 2 !.meas tran vout_pp PP V(output) FROM 1.5m TO 2m
